{"agent_id":"pp3g-PN60-create-detailed-crosslink-epic-for-observer-5b2f","agent_seq":8,"timestamp":"2026-08-27T00:41:20.326820639Z","event":{"type":"IssueUpdated","uuid":"ef06d5bc-07bc-4c5a-b42e-ab0411bf6808","description":"# EPIC: Observer — Centralized Operator Reports & Notification\n\nChosen design: **Hybrid F** — labels `observer` + `operator-report`, parent-epic grouping, and sentinel poll watcher. This combines three orthogonal surfaces for one filing action.\n\n## Hybrid F — Chosen Option\n\n| Surface | Role | Mechanism |\n|---------|------|-----------|\n| **Dual labels** `observer` + `operator-report` | Machine surface | `crosslink issue list -l observer -l operator-report` is the queryable backlog; label conjunction is the durable filter. |\n| **Parent epic grouping** | Human surface | Every operator-report issue sets `--parent <epic>` to this epic. The epic's sub-issue tree is the canonical human index (`crosslink issue show <epic>` → subissues). |\n| **Sentinel poll watcher** | Automation surface | Sentinel (or Observer daemon) polls `label=observer+operator-report` on cadence and sweeps into the durable store. Chosen over push-hook because Crosslink has no server-side label trigger; polling is the only mechanically available watcher until a hook surface exists. |\n\nFiling contract (one command):\n\n```\ncrosslink quick \"TITLE\" -p <pri> -l observer -l operator-report --parent <THIS_EPIC>\n```\n\nNo separate triage step — the two labels + parent are set at creation.\n\n## Observer Sweep — Every Issue → Knowledge Page Rule\n\nThe **Observer itself** monitors the Crosslink label conjunction `observer` + `operator-report` and sweeps matching issues into the durable git-tracked file:\n\n```\nknowledge/execution-engine-backlog.md\n```\n\nPer the *every issue → knowledge page* rule, Crosslink is the source of truth but git is the durability layer. The sweep preserves evidence per the **Workflow Topology** design (position-emitting agents + durable store + cheap staleness trigger; `docs/research/Workflow Topology Design and Reasoning Record.md`).\n\n* What the Observer does: on each poll, list issues with both labels, diff against the markdown table, append/update rows, commit. The file is the git-observable mirror; Crosslink remains authoritative for status/lifecycle.\n* Why both: labels survive only inside `issues.db`/hub; the markdown survives `git log`, review, and offline inspection.\n\n## Current Territory — #483–#487 Already Mirror There\n\nIssues #483–#487 occupy the same execution-engine durability territory and are already mirrored as the initial rows in `knowledge/execution-engine-backlog.md`:\n\n- #483 DOC: launch-resilience cadence (playbook + knowledge/launch-resilience.md)\n- #484 FEAT: crosslink-guard path-allowlist (child of #441)\n- #485 FEAT: crosslink-guard engine-backlog gate (child of #441)\n- #486 HOOK: orchestrator preflight — launch-resilience check\n- #487 FEAT: auto-export timer — push epics/issues to git on cadence (child of #441)\n\nFormal parents today are #441 (ases-tools thin CLI) where applicable; this epic is the **operator-notification view** over the same work. The backlog file groups them for operator triage regardless of formal parent.\n\nSync mechanism:\n- **Now:** manual sweep via `SESSION-END.md` handoff convention and ad-hoc Observer poll (operator/session-driven).\n- **Next:** auto-export timer #487 moves the sweep to a mechanical cadence (periodic `crosslink export` → markdown sync), removing the human step.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] **Filing is one command:** `crosslink quick` with `-l observer -l operator-report --parent <epic>` creates a correctly surfaced report.\n- [ ] **Central epic view is the human index:** `crosslink issue show <epic>` lists all operator reports as subissues; no separate dashboard needed for triage.\n- [ ] **Label poll is the machine surface:** `crosslink issue list -l observer -l operator-report` (or `--json`) returns exactly the operator backlog; sentinel/Observer poll consumes this conjunction.\n- [ ] **Observer sweep preserves evidence per workflow topology:** every labeled issue appears as a row in `knowledge/execution-engine-backlog.md`; the file is git-tracked, committed, and reconcilable against Crosslink; sweep is idempotent and preserves Workflow Topology's durable-store invariant.\n\n## Out of Scope\n\n- Changing Crosslink label semantics or adding server-side hooks (future work if a hook surface lands).\n- Re-parenting #483–#487 away from #441 — this epic provides a notification overlay, not a parent migration.\n\n## References\n\n- Workflow Topology Design and Reasoning Record (`docs/research/Workflow Topology Design and Reasoning Record.md`)\n- SESSION-END.md (current sync convention)\n- #487 auto-export timer (future mechanical sync)\n- #483, #484, #485, #486, #487 (initial backlog rows)\n- #441 ases-tools thin CLI (formal parent for #484/#485/#487)\n- #489 this epic's authoring issue"},"signed_by":"SHA256:d9TCn93YhXk5hp8RJEcEGrKzbH1dIoxvAChF0/jOato","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgXAU//9FJjnGtpJkHhy/tIqsrz03hrlv2jllLwq6u0lgAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQG8NGCeamjb6R/bvwaN3DDjC2y2DEXx36j6KoOi2B0QUM8pU6OmKreg95X069W+TWbG84r3gzib2IvuBBDDrlAc="}
